oss node1/node2/node3 (installed from GitHub binary release since no RHEL 9 package existed), loaded it with 5 application keys under /app/*, then simulated permanent loss of the node3 member (stopped etcd, ran `member remove` from the surviving quorum, and irrecoverably wiped /var/lib/etcd on node3). Replaced it with a fresh member on node3 using `member add` + ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=existing, which joined and fully synced all keys. Final cluster: 3 started members with matching raft term/index and all 5 keys present on every endpoint. Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured pre-restart boot IDs and healthy-service/data proof on all 3 nodes, restarted each node one at a time via native reboot (never more than one down simultaneously), confirmed changed boot IDs on all three, and verified full cluster health, membership, and data integrity after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Confirmed no etcd was pre-installed on any node (RHEL 9.8, no dnf package)\",\"Downloaded and installed etcd v3.5.17 (etcd/etcdctl/etcdutl) from GitHub releases on node1, node2, node3\",\"Created etcd system user, opened firewalld etcd-client/etcd-server services on all nodes\",\"Created systemd unit + /etc/etcd/etcd.conf on all 3 nodes and bootstrapped a new 3-member cluster (node1=10.100.60.10, node2=10.100.60.11, node3=10.100.60.12), enabled etcd for boot persistence\",\"Wrote 5 application keys under /app/config, /app/service, /app/secrets and verified replication to all 3 members including node3\",\"Simulated permanent loss of node3's member: stopped/disabled etcd on node3, ran `member remove` from node1 with quorum preserved on node1+node2, then wiped node3's data directory\",\"Verified cluster remained healthy (2/2 endpoints healthy) and all keys intact on survivors after removal\",\"Added a new member for node3 via `member add --peer-urls=...`, configured node3's etcd.conf with ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=existing and the updated member list, started etcd\",\"Verified the new node3 member joined, synced (matching raft term/index across all 3), and all 5 keys were present on node3\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and etcd health/data proof on all 3 nodes\",\"Rebooted node1, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, verified etcd active and cluster/data healthy\",\"Rebooted node2, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, verified etcd active and cluster/data healthy\",\"Rebooted node3, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, verified etcd active, full 3-member cluster health, matching raft indices, and all keys intact\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: 3-member cluster formed with application keys replicated to all members including node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-700a474bc12340ad\",\"cmd-671f3fba966a4abb\",\"cmd-322424b258ad4b94\"],\"summary\":\"member list shows 3 started members; 5 keys written and confirmed readable directly from node3's own endpoint before any disruption\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 member permanently lost: stopped, removed from cluster, data wiped irrecoverably\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3d55123c718f4f4f\",\"cmd-db861f2016a9439e\",\"cmd-efc450dc989e4d96\"],\"summary\":\"etcd stopped/disabled on node3; `member remove 74fe90394dbc065b` succeeded leaving 2 members (node1,node2); /var/lib/etcd on node3 shown empty after rm -rf\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cluster and data remained available on remaining quorum during the outage\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-07bccd78f7f9478d\"],\"summary\":\"node2 endpoint reports healthy and returns all 5 /app/* keys while node3 is down and removed\"},{\"requirement\":\"Replacement member added on node3 and rejoined cluster with data intact\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d6235041d79448af\",\"cmd-1cb3b18190494263\",\"cmd-bb7d083a686844c1\",\"cmd-5739a817fa474172\"],\"summary\":\"member add issued new member id 4fd65b7159c60698 for node3; etcd started active on node3; member list/endpoint status show 3 started members with identical raft term/index; node3 endpoint directly returns all 5 original keys\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-807d0baac99b48ab\",\"cmd-8c33624862164243\",\"cmd-93769e3cd53a4fe8\",\"cmd-6c8f95c23e044b3a\",\"cmd-a0885a04accc4f6e\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id c2f29441... captured pre-restart with etcd healthy/data present; reboot acknowledged; connection drop confirms disconnection; post-restart boot_id 9fae4555... (changed); cluster/member health and all keys reconfirmed\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8bb5f2c373864306\",\"cmd-ea85440c1d744579\",\"cmd-f3add9632e4b4137\",\"cmd-bae6ea08b59b4ce1\",\"cmd-1429a861b22d42d2\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id 6aa805ba... captured pre-restart with etcd healthy/data present; reboot acknowledged; post-restart boot_id 5e2e7b46... (changed); cluster/member health and all keys reconfirmed\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f9139291e6944a45\",\"cmd-1fbe4d3e81184ccc\",\"cmd-128d560b9662475f\",\"cmd-4a78ef631b194f7a\",\"cmd-e8d8f69fc96d4d2a\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id 377b5195... captured pre-restart (post member-replacement) with etcd healthy/data present; reboot acknowledged; post-restart boot_id 3c7d87f2... (changed); final full cluster health, matching raft term/index across all 3 members, and all 5 keys confirmed intact\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Built and validated a three-member etcd 3.5.17 cluster across node1/node2/node3 (installed from GitHub binary release since no RHEL 9 package existed), loaded it with 5 application keys under /app/*, then simulated permanent loss of the node3 member (stopped etcd, ran `member remove` from the surviving quorum, and irrecoverably wiped /var/lib/etcd on node3). Replaced it with a fresh member on node3 using `member add` + ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=existing, which joined and fully synced all keys. Final cluster: 3 started members with matching raft term/index and all 5 keys present on every endpoint. Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured pre-restart boot IDs and healthy-service/data proof on all 3 nodes, restarted each node one at a time via native reboot (never more than one down simultaneously), confirmed changed boot IDs on all three, and verified full cluster health, membership, and data integrity after each restart.","actions_performed":["Confirmed no etcd was pre-installed on any node (RHEL 9.8, no dnf package)","Downloaded and installed etcd v3.5.17 (etcd/etcdctl/etcdutl) from GitHub releases on node1, node2, node3","Created etcd system user, opened firewalld etcd-client/etcd-server services on all nodes","Created systemd unit + /etc/etcd/etcd.conf on all 3 nodes and bootstrapped a new 3-member cluster (node1=10.100.60.10, node2=10.100.60.11, node3=10.100.60.12), enabled etcd for boot persistence","Wrote 5 application keys under /app/config, /app/service, /app/secrets and verified replication to all 3 members including node3","Simulated permanent loss of node3's member: stopped/disabled etcd on node3, ran `member remove` from node1 with quorum preserved on node1+node2, then wiped node3's data directory","Verified cluster remained healthy (2/2 endpoints healthy) and all keys intact on survivors after removal","Added a new member for node3 via `member add --peer-urls=...`, configured node3's etcd.conf with ETCD_INITIAL_CLUSTER_STATE=existing and the updated member list, started etcd","Verified the new node3 member joined, synced (matching raft term/index across all 3), and all 5 keys were present on node3","Captured pre-restart boot_id and etcd health/data proof on all 3 nodes","Rebooted node1, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, verified etcd active and cluster/data healthy","Rebooted node2, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, verified etcd active and cluster/data healthy","Rebooted node3, polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, verified etcd active, full 3-member cluster health, matching raft indices, and all keys intact"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: 3-member cluster formed with application keys replicated to all members including node3","command_ids":["cmd-700a474bc12340ad","cmd-671f3fba966a4abb","cmd-322424b258ad4b94"],"summary":"member list shows 3 started members; 5 keys written and confirmed readable directly from node3's own endpoint before any disruption"},{"requirement":"node3 member permanently lost: stopped, removed from cluster, data wiped irrecoverably","command_ids":["cmd-3d55123c718f4f4f","cmd-db861f2016a9439e","cmd-efc450dc989e4d96"],"summary":"etcd stopped/disabled on node3; `member remove 74fe90394dbc065b` succeeded leaving 2 members (node1,node2); /var/lib/etcd on node3 shown empty after rm -rf"},{"requirement":"Cluster and data remained available on remaining quorum during the outage","command_ids":["cmd-07bccd78f7f9478d"],"summary":"node2 endpoint reports healthy and returns all 5 /app/* keys while node3 is down and removed"},{"requirement":"Replacement member added on node3 and rejoined cluster with data intact","command_ids":["cmd-d6235041d79448af","cmd-1cb3b18190494263","cmd-bb7d083a686844c1","cmd-5739a817fa474172"],"summary":"member add issued new member id 4fd65b7159c60698 for node3; etcd started active on node3; member list/endpoint status show 3 started members with identical raft term/index; node3 endpoint directly returns all 5 original keys"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-807d0baac99b48ab","cmd-8c33624862164243","cmd-93769e3cd53a4fe8","cmd-6c8f95c23e044b3a","cmd-a0885a04accc4f6e"],"summary":"boot_id c2f29441... captured pre-restart with etcd healthy/data present; reboot acknowledged; connection drop confirms disconnection; post-restart boot_id 9f